{"id":"20260827T012841.074972283Z-8af58ef0","time":"2026-08-27T01:28:41.074972283Z","session_id":"session-20260827T012434.071660249Z","task_id":"task-1787793874071825799","source":"architect","kind":"output","summary":"{\"decision\":\"proceed\",\"message\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Expose a concurrency-safe observational snapshot of Weighted state while preserving semaphore behavior.\",\"plan\":\"Add `(*Weighted).Stats() (weight int64, waiters int)` as a read-only snapshot taken under the existing mutex. Document that the values may become stale immediately and provide no synchronization guarantee. Preserve all acquisition, release, cancellation, fairness, and waiter-notification paths. Prove state transitions and concurrent observation through package tests and the race detector.\",\"steps\":[\"Add the documented `Stats` method, returning `cur` and `waiters.Len()` from one critical section under `mu`.\",\"Add deterministic tests covering empty, held, queued, awakened, canceled, and released states without inspecting private fields.\",\"Add a concurrency test that observes state while acquisitions and releases run, validating safe snapshots without prescribing scheduling.\",\"Run the semaphore package tests normally and with the race detector, then audit the final diff against Sensei.\"],\"consequences\":\"The semaphore package gains an exported observational API. Callers can inspect currently assigned weight and queued acquisitions, but cannot use the snapshot as a synchronization guarantee. Existing acquisition, release, cancellation, and fairness behavior remains unchanged.\",\"files\":[\"semaphore/semaphore.go\",\"semaphore/semaphore_test.go\"],\"mode\":\"modify\",\"related_invariants\":[],\"human_question\":\"\",\"recommendation\":\"\",\"options\":[],\"claims\":[{\"statement\":\"`Weighted.cur` records assigned weight and `Weighted.waiters` contains queued acquisition requests; existing accesses to both occur while `Weighted.mu` is held.\",\"about\":\"semaphore/semaphore.go: semaphore.Weighted\",\"source\":\"repository\"},{\"statement\":\"Successful acquisition increments `cur`; release and post-acquisition cancellation decrement it; queued entries are removed when awakened or canceled.\",\"about\":\"semaphore/semaphore.go: Acquire, Release, and notifyWaiters\",\"source\":\"repository\"},{\"statement\":\"A queued waiter is represented by an element in `waiters`, while oversized acquisitions waiting only for context cancellation are not queued.\",\"about\":\"semaphore/semaphore.go: Acquire\",\"source\":\"repository\"},{\"statement\":\"Existing semaphore tests exercise acquisition, release, cancellation, oversized requests, and starvation behavior through the public API.\",\"about\":\"semaphore/semaphore_test.go\",\"source\":\"repository\"},{\"statement\":\"The benchmark-only `weighted` interface deliberately contains only Acquire, TryAcquire, and Release, so adding a concrete method does not require changing it.\",\"about\":\"semaphore/semaphore_bench_test.go: weighted\",\"source\":\"repository\"},{\"statement\":\"Sensei classifies the indexed implementation file as low-risk with local blast radius and no approval gate, while the test file remains unindexed with unknown impact.\",\"about\":\"semaphore/semaphore.go and semaphore/semaphore_test.go\",\"source\":\"graph\"},{\"statement\":\"Sensei found no active invariant, forbidden fix, or required test directly governing the planned files; its public API contract entry is candidate-only.\",\"about\":\"component.semaphore and contract.library_api.semaphore\",\"source\":\"graph\"},{\"statement\":\"The same-mutex read provides a mutually consistent instantaneous pair, but the pair may become stale as soon as the mutex is released and cannot coordinate caller actions.\",\"about\":\"proposed Weighted.Stats semantics\",\"source\":\"inference\"},{\"statement\":\"Task-aware briefing could not run because the tool returned exactly: `Mcp error: -32000: no task session exists in this repository`.\",\"about\":\"Sensei task state\",\"source\":\"graph\"}]}","payload":{"stream":"assistant"}}
